WEBVTT

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:41.290
What's the idea?

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.070
You can't climb a plane straight up.

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:44.090
She'll conk out every time.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:44.960
I know, Bob.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.240
I just thought I'd try a web stall.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:47.990
Well, you stick a straight fly, Miss Miller,

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:49.050
until you've had more hours.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.070
You don't have a good mind not to send your papers

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:51.750
through for your license.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:53.820
I pulled out of the spin, didn't I?

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.580
I did remember everything you told me.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.080
Well, sure, but you barely made it.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.980
Oh, Bob, I've got to have that license today.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:01.120
I've just got to.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:02.160
I see.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.180
You've already told your father.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.140
Now you must make good.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.150
Well, there's one reason.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:08.590
Bob, do I get the license?

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:11.100
Yes.

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:24.140
Where shall I hold the receiver, Dr. Miller?

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.920
Halfway across the room, Dr. Halsey.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.640
We'll shorten the distance and hope for better results.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:40.470
What is it, my dear?

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:41.220
It.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.200
Made it?

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:42.700
Made what?

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.000
My pilot's license.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:44.920
Don't you remember?

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.140
I wanted to have it today to surprise Jim.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:48.020
Oh, of course.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:48.780
I've forgotten.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:49.440
I'm sorry.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:51.220
Oh, I'm the one who should be.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:51.680
Sorry.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.640
I came bursting in on something important, didn't I?

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:54.720
Oh, that's all right.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.800
You and Dr. House go right ahead, Deb.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.450
Mind if I watch until Jim comes?

00:02:58.670 --> 00:02:59.910
Certainly not, my dear.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:00.780
Certainly not.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:05.440
That must be Jim.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:06.140
Turn it off.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.760
Well, well, how are you, my lad?

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:16.460
Fine, sir.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:17.660
I thought you were in uniform.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:18.320
Well, I was.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:19.480
I have a medical discharge.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:20.520
Medical discharge.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:21.880
Father, don't you remember?

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.980
I told you, Jim was wounded at Guadalcanal

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.320
flying for the Marines and cited for bravery, too.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.100
Of course, of course.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.820
Oh, I beg your pardon, doctor.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:30.980
This is Jim Hudson.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.900
Jim's Dr. Howe, Dad's assistant.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:33.320
Hello.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:34.140
How do you do?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.520
Jim is the son of one of my best friends, old Warren Bill Hudson,

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.730
owner of a famous gun side mine in Alaska.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.000
Well, what are you working on, sir?

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:44.140
We're attempting to transmit physical substance by light wave.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.560
We almost have it, but so far we've been unable to hit upon an element

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.760
strong enough or powerful enough to counteract the pull of gravity.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:51.760
Well, that's amazing.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.100
I call it the peritone.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:56.790
Well, would you mind very much, sir, if I stayed and watched you work?

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:57.610
Not at all.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.080
You and Ruth stand over there.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:03:59.820
Well, thank you, sir.

00:04:56.236 --> 00:04:58.236
and then it slips from our grasp.

00:04:58.604 --> 00:04:59.604
find the proper element.

00:05:00.444 --> 00:05:01.684
proper atomic combination.

00:05:02.876 --> 00:05:03.716
I've tried everything.

00:05:04.252 --> 00:05:05.412
I don't know where to go from here.

00:05:06.364 --> 00:05:10.404
Well, could it be possible, Doctor, that the substance you're looking for is in mineral form?

00:05:10.644 --> 00:05:11.044
Naturally.

00:05:11.484 --> 00:05:13.544
Radium is mineral and that has energy.

00:05:14.108 --> 00:05:15.668
but not the particular type I need.

00:05:15.932 --> 00:05:16.712
Well, that's what I meant.

00:05:17.404 --> 00:05:18.024
What, Radium?

00:05:18.396 --> 00:05:22.496
No, not exactly. It's something Pop wrote me about when I was on Guadalcanal.

00:05:22.972 --> 00:05:25.832
Now, he hasn't told anyone else about it because he thinks he's got a great discovery.

00:05:26.428 --> 00:05:27.428
Well, what is it?

00:05:28.348 --> 00:05:29.648
Well, I can only tell you that...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.760
You remember old Grit Pops Foreman?

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:32.380
Mm-hmm.

00:05:32.656 --> 00:05:35.036
Well, he was digging in number three shaft one day last spring,

00:05:35.076 --> 00:05:37.576
and he came across this mysterious substance, whatever it is,

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:39.736
and he hit it with his pig, and it knocked him down.

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:40.812
Downing.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.240
Could you arrange to have a sample sent to us?

00:05:43.628 --> 00:05:44.788
It may be just what we need.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.820
Well, it sounds like it'd be a little too dangerous for shipment.

00:05:48.268 --> 00:05:50.028
Why don't you go north with Jim, Dad?

00:05:50.284 --> 00:05:52.784
Even though there's nothing to it, you'll have a nice vacation.

00:05:53.324 --> 00:05:54.244
You need a rent.

00:05:54.364 --> 00:05:55.324
Well, how about that, Doctor?

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.060
Well, if the story is true, I feel it's our duty.

00:05:58.796 --> 00:05:59.996
Do you have a place where you could work?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.170
Well, yes, you remember Pop's lab.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:03.190
It's about as big as this.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:03.870
Oh, excellent.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:04.930
When can we start?

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:07.330
I won't arrest him's life and find out what this is all about.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:09.370
Well, transportation's the big problem.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:10.830
How much of this equipment do you have to take?

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:12.630
Well, all this apparatus is necessary.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:16.640
If I may offer a suggestion, there's a team ship leaving from here in two days.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:19.020
And the captain is a very good friend of mine.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:20.260
Well, then that's fine.

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:23.140
You arrange the transportation, and I'll help Dr. Miller get things together.

00:07:04.572 --> 00:07:05.812
Just got word from headquarters.

00:07:06.268 --> 00:07:08.188
We're going through with everything the way I wanted it.

00:07:08.348 --> 00:07:11.308
But I've told you the real secret of the invention is only known to Miller.

00:07:11.676 --> 00:07:13.496
Thought you said you could figure this parrot one out.

00:07:14.012 --> 00:07:15.332
You could take it apart and examine it.

00:07:15.964 --> 00:07:16.804
to what I could.

00:07:32.972 --> 00:07:33.692
Why don't we sail?

00:07:34.156 --> 00:07:35.536
I don't know. I must be waiting on somebody.

00:07:36.684 --> 00:07:39.864
I'll give them guys five more minutes, boss, and if they ain't here, then we'll slam.

00:07:40.164 --> 00:07:40.664
Aye, sir.

00:07:40.908 --> 00:07:41.368
Hi, Doc.

00:07:42.956 --> 00:07:45.056
Sorry to have missed you yesterday, but I was busy ashore.

00:07:45.156 --> 00:07:47.356
Captain Greeter, I would like you to meet Dr. Miller.

00:07:47.456 --> 00:07:48.256
How do you do, sir?

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.540
And Mr. Hudson, come on.

00:07:49.772 --> 00:07:50.772
Oh, here they are, Sid.

00:07:55.724 --> 00:07:56.424
this gangplank.

00:07:56.716 --> 00:07:57.456
We're coming up.

00:07:59.596 --> 00:07:59.996
check with

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:01.880
and see where our cabin is.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:02.160
Yeah.

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:26.680
Sign of that fog lifting?

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:27.740
No, Captain.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:29.640
I think we ought to lay to until it does.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.590
This is the season for icebergs.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.340
No, we're too far south for Bergs.

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:36.830
Keep her steady as she goes.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:38.330
Aye, aye.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:40.840
What's the matter? You nervous, Dr. House?

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.440
Well, it's two men who came aboard.

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:43.770
I wonder who they are.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.590
They're really keep to themselves, don't they?

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:49.290
Only time they come out of that cabin is to walk the dog.

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:51.910
You worried about them?

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:53.220
Tams like these.

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:55.150
The important nature of our work.

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:56.270
I'm suspicious of everyone.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:58.500
I think I'll take a walk on deck.

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:15.530
really jumpy, isn't he? Is he? I haven't noticed. How well do you know Dr. House? He was well

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:22.870
recommended. Well, are you sure of him? Well, he's never sure of anything, at least of all of men.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:28.710
But don't worry. The real secret of the Perich Arm is known only to me.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:32.620
You're not as absent-minded as you seem to be, are you?

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:38.340
There's no telling who or what they might be.

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:41.210
If Miller and Hudson were murdered crudely.

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:42.550
What do you mean, crudely?

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:44.190
Ain't you ever heard of an accident?

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:46.250
When will this accident happen?

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.600
As soon as we get further north out of the sea lane.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:49.960
You happy now?

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:51.930
Scientist captain is seldom happy.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:56.160
Oh, captain, I advise you to check on those two men

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.080
and find out who they are.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:59.980
As far as I know, they're just two guys named Gray and Dunn.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:02.800
Are you sure the American secret agent are not catching up with you?

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:07.520
You know, this ship has a bad reputation ever since those two miners disappeared overboard last month.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.890
I'll keep an eye on them. See what you can find out, too.

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:22.570
They're passing iceboards all evening, Captain. And that means icebergs.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:28.480
Day 2 in the morning.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:29.180
Aye, aye, sir.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:49.590
the captain has carrier pigeons on board and it's keeping it a secret i don't know carrier

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:54.100
pigeons are a respectable hobby maybe so but we were wondering why greeter doesn't send his

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:58.970
messages by radio probably part of his hobby that seemed kind of strange though didn't it

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.650
Well, I wouldn't give it a thought.

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:03.910
Well, gentlemen, I'm tired.

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:06.750
I think I'll take a little walk around the deck and then go to bed.

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:08.950
Well, I thought you'd like to know.

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:09.810
Yeah, well, thanks, Don.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:13.210
Don discovered the pigeon.

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:14.980
I saw you send a message.

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:17.400
You sure know that he is an American agent.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:20.660
You go back to your cabin.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:21.400
I'll handle this.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:36.500
Hiya, Dunn.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:37.340
Howdy, Captain.

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:39.780
I'd like to have a little talk with you, if you don't mind.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:40.540
Sure.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:50.580
Hi, Dunn.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.420
We're back here.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.840
Speak right up and tell me what you're doing on board my ship.

00:12:57.310 --> 00:12:58.250
I'm going up north.

00:12:58.450 --> 00:12:59.490
Anything wrong with that?

00:12:59.690 --> 00:12:59.930
Never.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.400
Since you came on board, you've been snooping around.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:07.120
You got something to hide, Captain, like maybe carrier pigeons?

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:08.360
Listen, you.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:10.140
Tell me who you are or...

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:10.760
What?

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:39.280
We're proceeding at 5 knots, Bosun.

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:42.080
Captain, you can't move with them icebergs out there.

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:43.660
I'm giving the orders here.

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:51.560
You looked everywhere for it, Don. I tell you, there's something wrong with this boat.

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:53.470
Oh, sit down. Take it easy. He'll show you.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.170
He's most likely with the captain.

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:58.130
No, I was on the bridge. The Bosun says there's no one with the captain.

00:13:58.980 --> 00:13:59.960
The captain had better be towed.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.000
Perhaps we should see him this minute.

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:04.290
The ship must be searched from top to bottom.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:04.880
Thanks.

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:07.040
I'm moving again.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.480
I tell you, whoever's running this boat is crazy.

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:18.660
What happened to Dunn?

00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:20.290
I've heaved him over the side.

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:22.190
Miller and Hudson already suspect something.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:24.180
When they missed them, they'll call for an investigation.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:25.600
What's the difference?

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.610
It means we've got to work right now.

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:29.280
Now?

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:31.870
Go below and send Miller Gray and Hudson up to me.

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:32.830
Oh, not that way.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:34.280
You know a better way?

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:37.220
Yes. And this is dissolved in water.

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:39.040
It releases a deadly gas.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:40.440
Won't they see it?

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:40.760
No.

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:42.290
Colorless and odorless.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:44.930
Now, if you could manage to lock them up in here.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:46.180
Leave that to me.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:46.920
Send them up.

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:54.820
Don't be too hasty in accusing the Captain Mr. Gray

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:56.160
as a friend of Dr. Howe, you know.

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:58.380
The Captain would like to see you, gentlemen.

00:14:58.880 --> 00:14:59.980
Actually, he's very much concerned.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:24.040
sir you'll get some action does he want me to yes doctor a matter of routine i believe the fact

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:28.820
that there's a passenger missing from my ship i'm gonna hold you free until i get to the bottom of

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:29.590
this clever

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:38.630
Captain we don't know anything about it where it's all ridiculous gentlemen make yourselves comfortable until I get back

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:56.080
Then there's a frame-up

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:02.060
Got the paratron?

00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:02.660
Yes.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:04.060
They're out upon his notes.

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:06.500
Perhaps the secret of the paratron is among them.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:00.620
Come back here and wait.

00:17:00.820 --> 00:17:01.720
Call her a lot, folks.
